card.statement:
Given $T(Q)$ and $T(R)$ in $\mathcal{B}(T(L))$, we write $T(R)\preceq_{(1)}T(Q)$ if there exist $g\in\mathfrak{gl}(n)$ such that $T(Q)$ appears with nonzero coef\/f\/icient in the decomposition of $g\cdot T(R)$ into a linear combination of tableaux. For any $p\geq 1$ we write $T(R)\preceq_{(p)} T(Q)$ if there exist tableaux $T(L^{(1)})$,\dots, $T(L^{(p)})$, such that

\begin{gather*}
T(R)=T\big(L^{(0)}\big)\preceq_{(1)}T\big(L^{(1)}\big)\preceq_{(1)}\cdots\preceq_{(1)}T\big(L^{(p)}\big)=T(Q).
\end{gather*}
